FOUNDERS LEDGER
Sunday, September 13, 2026 | Edition 89

Good morning. Four things this week.

1) ROUNDS WE NOTICED
- Saltmarsh Software (Portland) raised a $22M Series A led by Palisade Growth for property-management accounting.
- Hexley Materials (Pittsburgh) closed a $40M Series B led by Granite Peak Ventures for recycled-alloy production.
- Nightjar Security (Austin) raised a $7M seed from Alder Lane Ventures for identity tooling aimed at mid-sized companies.
- Juniper Grid (Denver) announced a $65M Series B led by Cormorant Capital for distribution-grid software.

2) TERM SHEET WATCH
Founder secondaries at the Series A are back. Six of the 28 term sheets we saw this month allowed founders to sell between $500K and $1.5M of common as part of the round, typically capped at 10% of the founder's holdings. Two years ago this was a Series B conversation. The leads offering it say the same thing: a founder who has paid off the mortgage makes better long-term decisions. Ask; the worst answer is no.

3) CHART OF THE WEEK
Share of US Series A dollars by category, trailing twelve months: AI application-layer companies took 41%, up from 28% a year ago; infrastructure and developer tools 17%; vertical software 15%; everything else 27%. Chart: https://foundersledger.com/charts/series-a-by-category-2026

4) WORTH READING
"The data room that closed in eleven days," a practical piece on what a lead's associate actually opens first, and the three documents that generate the most follow-up questions. https://foundersledger.com/reads/eleven-day-data-room

Have a good Sunday.
Colette

